# 1v1, cloud locks to the PC (BENCH-253), round 5: every per-robot line that locked on the cloud (24 fresh seeds pooled,
# 95% low end above 0, live turn time; coverage/shards/locks.tsv) after round 4 (PR #866) ran, locked on 12 fresh PC seeds:
#   vj (MOVE-44 velocity jitter): Welby +2.2 (low +1.4)
#   hl (MOVE-28 stop-and-start): Dorito +1.0 (+0.35), KnackOnOne +0.75 (+0.07), Thinker +1.0 (+0.01)
#   dp (DIST-4 distance pin): RedShift pinned at 550 px +0.4 (+0.01)
#   kl (SKEY-2 surf key): Insomnia +2.6 (+1.2, 12 seeds)
#   KnackOnOne, Thinker and RedShift only just clear 0 over 24 cloud seeds; the PC decides them.
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live
#   lock       the 6 robots   c / aa / vj / hl / dp / kl (each lever arm built with only its own robots)   12 fresh seeds
#              from 43500, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks5 (earlier rounds' battles stay in work/pc-locks to -locks4)
#   gate       each robot judged on its own arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95% low end
#              is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0)
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 4 left this plan's queue state marked complete; an interrupted round 5 resumes without it.
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 432 lock battles (6 robots, 6 arms, 12 seeds), about 14 minutes
# with the live-match check.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: every line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master.
#   - Diagnosis first (shards G and C, easy-band move lanes, truth logs against Saguaro 1.1.4 and BeepBoop 2.0):
#     vj: Welby hits us 3.5% of its shots, Saguaro 2.4%, BeepBoop 0.6%, worst at walls and mid speed; it locks on our
#     exact velocity, and the jitter of MOVE-44 (held on the PC for Booring and AspidReloaded) breaks the match.
#     hl: our still ticks take 16% hits from Dorito and 4.3% from KnackOnOne, where Saguaro takes none; stop-and-start
#     moves us off the still positions their guns read. Thinker screened +2.1 on the same lever.
#     dp: 65% of our extra hits from RedShift over Saguaro land at 200-350 px; the pin holds us at 550 px.
#     kl: a surf key fitted offline from Insomnia's own bullets (data/tools/surf_key_fit.py, shard M) reweights our
#     surf's hit views for it alone; it locked +2.6 (low +1.2) over 12 fresh cloud seeds. 175 such keys held +0.06 APS on the PC (BENCH-160).
#   - Every robot passed the cloud lock bar first; round 3 held 17 of 25 (#860), round 4 held 5 of 6 (#866).
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): the watcher's A/A rule needs 10 robots read in both c and aa, which this 6-robot
# lock never reaches; aa is read in the gate (multiarm.py prints aa against c). The card halts on 30 failed
# battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24, or no battle in 30 minutes. The
# live-match step stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
# Bank: the owning cloud thread adds the gate's lines on this card's results PR. Nothing is released by the card.
set V = 3.23
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks5
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in vj hl dp kl; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out work/pc-livematch-rel-live --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py work/pc-livematch-rel-live/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks5-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 12 --seed-base 43500 --arms ${W}-prep/lock.arms --out ${W} --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks5-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks5-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks5-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms vj hl dp kl --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks5-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks5-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks5-results "1v1 cloud locks, round 5 (6 robots from the field shards) locked on 12 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks5-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks5-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks5-lock-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks5-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
